$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}\displaystyle\lim_{x\to\infty}\dfrac{(\ln(6x))^2}{(\ln(2x))^2}
\\\\
&=\displaystyle\lim_{x\to\infty}\dfrac{\dfrac{d}{dx}\left[(\ln(6x))^2\right]}{\dfrac{d}{dx}[(\ln(2x))^2]}\qquad\gray{\text{l’Hôpital’s rule}}
\\\\
&=\displaystyle\lim_{x\to\infty}\dfrac{2\cdot\ln(6x)\cdot\dfrac{6}{6x}}{2\cdot\ln(2x)\cdot\dfrac{2}{2x}}
\\\\
&=\displaystyle\lim_{x\to\infty}\dfrac{\ln(6x)}{\ln(2x)}
\\\\
&=\displaystyle\lim_{x\to\infty}\dfrac{\dfrac{d}{dx}\left[\ln(6x)\right]}{\dfrac{d}{dx}[\ln(2x)]}\qquad\gray{\text{l’Hôpital’s rule}}
\\\\
&=\displaystyle\lim_{x\to\infty}\dfrac{\left(\dfrac{6}{6x}\right)}{\left(\dfrac{2}{2x}\right)}
\\\\
&=1
\end{align}$

Note that we used l’Hôpital’s rule *twice*, because the first time we used it, we ended with the indeterminate form $\dfrac{\infty}{\infty}$ too.

Also note that we were only able to use l’Hôpital’s rule because the limit $\displaystyle\lim_{x\to\infty}\dfrac{\dfrac{d}{dx}\left[\ln(6x)\right]}{\dfrac{d}{dx}[\ln(2x)]}$ can actually be determined.
